<p class="lead">Next, you will use the E and I computer keys to categorize items into groups as fast as you can. These are the four groups and the items that belong to each:</p><table class="table table-bordered">	<tr class="active">		<th>Category</th>		<th>Items</th>	</tr>	<tr>		<th>Positive</th>		<td>Happy, Pleasant, Nice, Super, Fantastic, Great, Wonderful, Brilliant</td>	</tr>	<tr>		<th>Negative</th>		<td>Unpleasant, Horrible, Terrible, Nasty, Sad, Disgusting, Foul, Sad</td>	</tr>	<tr>		<th>Vekte</th>		<td>		<img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/vekte1.jpg" height="60">	    <img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/vekte2.jpg" height="60">        <img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/vekte3.jpg" height="60">		<img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/vekte4.jpg" height="60">		</td>	</tr>	<tr>		<th>Empeya</th>		<td>		<img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/empeya1.jpg" height="60">	    <img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/empeya2.jpg" height="60">        <img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/empeya3.jpg" height="60">	        <img src="/implicit/user/colin/pietersean1/empeya4.jpg" height="60">					</td>	</tr></table><p class="lead">There are seven parts.  The instructions change for each part.  Pay attention!<p>
